May I submit the following for the collective review of the readers of
this newsgroup.  Perhaps the authors of the WCST spoilers will see fit to
include this information is a future edition (subject of course to any
changes or corrections).

When you #offer a unicorn corpse, it is treated differently than most
other types of corpses.  There are two special cases:
 1. Sacrificing a unicorn on an altar of the same alignment as the
    unicorn is a BAD idea.  The god of that alignment will get very
    angry and possibly kill you.  (Does anything special happen if it
    also happens to be your alignment?)
 2. Sacrificing a unicorn of your own alignment on an altar of another
    alignment will cause your character to change to the alignment of
    the altar.
Other than the above two cases (i.e. when unicorn ^= altar and
unicorn ^= character), sacrificing a unicorn works pretty much the same
as sacrificing any other kind of corpse.

(For the uninitiated, the alignment of a unicorn can be determined from
its color:  white = lawful; gray = neutral; black = chaotic.)


